# First blessing approved by the maintainer on 2026-10-05 for #134.
# Chapter 6: no matching internal error clause means no unhandled report;
# an error Run that errors again ends errored but sends no further message.
# Without any error clauses, dispatch spends no Fuel and starts no Run.
# A Host-delivered error is an ordinary Delivery: during is Nothing, no match
# reports unhandled, and an uncaught error still does not chain.
# A limit fault and an unhandled ordinary message also send no error message.

